<h2 id="quick-answer">What should a first time dad know?</h2>
<p><strong>Start participating before the baby arrives. Support your partner, learn basic baby care, make a practical money and leave plan, and talk about the first days home. You do not need to feel ready for everything. You need to keep learning, share the work, and ask for help when you need it.</strong></p>
<p>This is the list we would want in our pocket before becoming dads. Not twenty one products. Not a speech about how fast it goes. The practical stuff that changes a Tuesday night when everyone is tired and nobody can find the clean burp cloths.</p>
<p>At Dudela, we organize preparation around six pillars: your head, your money, your partnership, birth, the kind of dad you want to be, and the first days home. This guide follows that same idea. Read it once, then choose a few things to act on. You do not need twenty one new assignments tonight.</p>
